<h1>Bone Daddies — Leicester Square</h1>

<p>
<strong>Category:</strong> Ramen<br>
<strong>Area:</strong> Leicester Square<br>
<strong>Visited:</strong> February 2026<br>
<strong>Price:</strong> £15–£18<br>
<strong>Rating:</strong> 7.5/10
</p>

<hr>

<h2>Overview</h2>

<p>
Bone Daddies is a well-known London ramen chain located just off Leicester Square.
The atmosphere is energetic and loud, with fast service and strong flavours.
</p>

<h2>Broth</h2>

<p>
Rich and salty tonkotsu broth with strong umami. Slightly heavier than traditional Hakata style.
</p>

<h2>Noodles</h2>

<p>
Good firmness and texture. Holds up well in the broth.
</p>

<h2>Toppings</h2>

<p>
Chashu is flavourful but thinner than premium ramen specialists. Egg is well marinated.
</p>

<h2>Atmosphere</h2>

<p>
Busy, loud, and casual. More modern London ramen vibe rather than traditional Japanese setting.
</p>

<h2>Verdict</h2>

<p>
Solid ramen option in central London. Convenient location, strong flavours, but not the most authentic compared to specialist shops.
</p>

<hr>

<p>
<strong>Pros:</strong><br>
• Strong flavour<br>
• Central location<br>
• Fast service
</p>

<p>
<strong>Cons:</strong><br>
• Slightly too salty<br>
• Less refined than top-tier ramen spots
</p>

